#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073486 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073716 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aabbe3f2-c799-5d31-b5c1-8d21b32afccc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Division Problem Represented by a Model"}] :question/id #uuid "4fae5cf1-65c9-5217-89ec-54b40e80f293" :question/math-academy-id "e-14418" :question/problem "What division problem is represented by the model below?\n\n![](images/b2/b2e5fb40e703cb3d93f22fd315852930eaab540445e3f570e8de3dacfdc83e0b.png)" :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{4}\n$$\n\non the left and\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{8}\n$$\n\non the right.\n\n![](images/78/785deacac749a6ed43e5e6a2638677e8ff9e9b58087cb4e471ea85fd50609ce6.png)\n\nThe division operation splits the shaded region on the left into $2$ equal parts. So the shaded part on the left is $2$ times larger than the shaded part on the right.\n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{4} \\div 2 = \\dfrac{1}{8}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073487 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073717 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91201453-ec4d-55a4-8a7b-eae34fca9f8d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Missing Divisor in a Division Model"}] :question/id #uuid "9cd2d717-01de-5319-8759-2990e79d64ad" :question/math-academy-id "e-14420" :question/problem "What number is missing from the division problem below?\n\n![](images/cf/cf2500f82f337e5635a5ca9854579e3b883f42cde4598d4324c94364bf998a0d.png)" :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3}\n$$\n\non the left and\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{15}\n$$\n\non the right.\n\n![](images/ed/ed5517a9242aed1c5b521ca07772dacbb7c96a73c69d4d9c6214a098742358e2.png)\n\nThe division operation splits the shaded region on the left into $5$ equal parts. So the shaded part on the left is $5$ times larger than the shaded part on the right.\n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3} \\div {\\color{blue}{5}} = \\dfrac{1}{15}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $\\color{blue}5$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073488 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073718 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bb96a84-3329-5702-ae45-a7d0ad2a95c6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Missing Result in a Division Model"}] :question/id #uuid "62d9f262-e419-5a9d-a5cb-741c34613570" :question/math-academy-id "e-14423" :question/problem "What picture is missing from the division model below?\n\n![](images/9c/9cc5d672cb3c12ceb7704f5136e9b7ecae61d11a9418acf3b8e1cbb9e8f044f7.png)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that in the model, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3}\n$$\n\non the left.\n\nSince we need to divide by $\\color{blue}3$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}3$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/30/30f9bbc604d35a9a15e1418c0cf80eca87fe4d704287c15fb8de7426eb9e3de9.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{9}\n$$\n\nof the whole.\n\nSo, the missing picture is:\n\n![](images/95/951a4bc0607c53aa0c5ed9cebe664b630acf226a6f9844fd9d1b8e6ae952d0ed.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073489 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a903aacb-718a-52f6-8be7-a7043358b7bb" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Model to Solve a Division Problem"}] :question/id #uuid "c6e1860a-9fe5-559c-8a19-6ed98335659b" :question/math-academy-id "e-14424" :question/problem "Use the model below to calculate $\\dfrac{1}{4} \\div 4$.\n\n![](images/8e/8eccf163bffabb43593188590a1f995544f3d1ac0aebcdd87dce638b230f8165.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since we need to divide by $\\color{blue}4$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}4$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/a3/a34a3fb198ef2ea79f8baf8f0acbdbdc179c6259c614824315d3d96e5ea4e921.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{16}\n$$\n\nof the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{4} \\div 4 = \\dfrac{1}{16}\\,\n$$"}]}
